### 6. Color Through Character Intensity

**Grayscale Values:**
```
Black:    ████████ (Highest contrast)
Dark:     ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ (Strong emphasis)
Medium:   ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒ (Medium emphasis)
Light:    ░░░░░░░░ (Subtle backgrounds)
White:    ........ (Text space)
```

**Usage Guidelines:**
- Use heavy characters (`█▓`) for primary elements
- Medium characters (`▒░`) for secondary/background elements
- Reserve light characters for subtle divisions
- Create contrast through character density, not just symbols

